# AI Request Sequence

Below is a sequence diagram showing a user's browser request flowing through a web server, a LangChain agent (which may call tools), and an Ollama server hosting the AI model.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
	participant Browser as User Browser
	participant Server as Web Server
	participant LangChain as LangChain Agent
	participant Tools as External Tools
	participant Ollama as Ollama Server (AI Model)

	Browser->>Server: POST /api/ai-request (input + metadata)
	Server->>LangChain: build_prompt(input) + tool_descriptions
	alt Tool needed
		LangChain->>Tools: call tool (e.g., search, DB)
		Tools-->>LangChain: tool result
	end
	LangChain->>Ollama: model.invoke(prompt + tool_results)
	loop Streaming tokens
		Ollama-->>LangChain: token chunk (stream)
		LangChain-->>Server: forward stream (SSE/WebSocket)
		Server-->>Browser: stream tokens
	end
	Ollama-->>LangChain: final response
	LangChain-->>Server: structured response (answer + citations)
	Server-->>Browser: 200 OK (answer)

	alt Error path
		Ollama-->>LangChain: error
		LangChain-->>Server: error payload
		Server-->>Browser: 5xx / error JSON
	end
```

Notes:
- LangChain can orchestrate tool calls before or during model calls (tool usage shown in the "Tool needed" branch).
- Streaming shows token chunks flowing from Ollama through LangChain and the server to the browser (SSE/WebSocket).

